Done. `dispatch` now validates `maxAttempts` (default 3) and `baseDelayMs` (default 100) upfront, retries each job up to `maxAttempts` with `sleep(baseDelayMs * 2 ** (attempt - 1))` between failures, and records `attempts` on every processed/failed entry. Only the final outcome is logged, one line per job. Added injected-sleep tests for retry-then-success, exhaustion, backoff delays, and pre-dequeue validation — `node --test` passes 32/32.
